 ## Background
-Surface Curvature Regularization originates from the need to improve the smoothness and quality of neural implicit surface reconstructions [S2, unofficial]. It was notably employed in **Neuralangelo** [S1] to regularize the mean curvature of SDFs computed via discrete Laplacian, addressing issues with hash encoding gradients. It was also explored in **VolSDF** [S2, unofficial] where Gaussian and Mean curvatures were computed analytically to regularize the surface directly. The method addresses the tendency of unregularized neural implicit surfaces to exhibit noise and sharp, unnatural transitions.
